claim.claim-text:
a housing (210) including a front surface and a rear surface opposite to the first surface, the housing including a first periphery, a second periphery opposite to and parallel with the first periphery, a third periphery longer than and substantially perpendicular to the first periphery and the second periphery, and a fourth periphery opposite to and parallel with the third periphery;
a first display (261) disposed in the housing and visible through the front surface, the first display (261) having a first size and a first resolution;
a second display (262b) at least partially disposed between the first display (261) and a first portion of the rear surface when viewed in a first direction substantially parallel to the rear surface, the second display (262b) being visible through the first portion of the rear surface and having a second size smaller than the first size and a second resolution different from the first resolution;
a near field communication (NFC) antenna (397) at least partially disposed between the first display (261) and a second portion of the rear surface when viewed in the first direction;
a plurality of camera modules (380) at least partially disposed between the first display (261) and a third portion of the rear surface when viewed in the first direction, and visible through the third portion of the rear surface; and
a flash (381) at least partially disposed between the first display (261) and a fourth portion of the rear surface when viewed in the first direction, and visible through the fourth portion of the rear surface,
wherein the NFC antenna (397) is at least partially disposed between the second display (262b) and the first periphery, when viewed in a direction substantially perpendicular to the rear surface,
wherein the plurality of camera modules (180) are at least partially disposed between the second display (262b) and the third periphery, when viewed in the second direction, and
wherein the flash (181) is at least partially disposed between the second display (262b) and the third periphery, when viewed in the second direction.
